From: Kevin Liu <11365056+kliu128@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: clear the host memory region of the firmware

On targets with a fixed memory region the HOST_DDR region is mapped and
handed to the firmware as it is. After a firmware restart it still holds
the data of the previous firmware instance.

Clear it every time it is assigned.

Signed-off-by: Kevin Liu <11365056+kliu128@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/qmi.c
@@ -2067,6 +2067,14 @@
 					ab->qmi.target_mem[i].size);
 			if (!ab->qmi.target_mem[idx].iaddr)
 				return -EIO;
+
+			/*
+			 * The firmware expects this region to be clear. After
+			 * a firmware restart it still holds what the previous
+			 * instance left behind.
+			 */
+			memset_io(ab->qmi.target_mem[idx].iaddr, 0,
+				  ab->qmi.target_mem[i].size);
 
 			ab->qmi.target_mem[idx].size = ab->qmi.target_mem[i].size;
 			host_ddr_sz = ab->qmi.target_mem[i].size;
